## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design cross-region consistency with SLA targets and fault tolerance for multi-tenant streams.

## Key Concepts
- Total order per tenant across regions
- Vector clocks and regional sequence numbers
- Barrier commits, idempotent processing, and tombstones
- Fault injection and late-arrival handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vector clock merge for per-tenant streams
function mergeVC(a, b) {
  const keys = new Set([...Object.keys(a), ...Object.keys(b)]);
  const out = {};
  for (const k of keys) {
    out[k] = Math.max(a[k] || 0, b[k] || 0);
  }
  return out;
}

// Regional sequencer generates monotonically increasing sequence
class RegionalSequencer {
  constructor(region) {
    this.region = region;
    this.sequences = new Map(); // tenantId -> sequence number
  }

  next(tenantId) {
    const current = this.sequences.get(tenantId) || 0;
    const next = current + 1;
    this.sequences.set(tenantId, next);
    return { tenantId, sequence: next, region: this.region };
  }
}
```

Why This Is Asked
